        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0914df20-88b7-5029-82fb-80b6bdd8e269",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions, WED Enterprises\n- People: Walt Disney, Esther Forbes\n- Products: Johnny Tremain (film), Magic Kingdom, Disneyland Park\n- Places: Boston, Massachusetts, Anaheim, California\n- Topics: American Revolution, fairy tales, Disney characters\n\nFacts:\n- Esther Forbes wrote the 1944 Newbery Medal-winning children's novel Johnny Tremain.\n- Johnny Tremain is a 1957 film made by Walt Disney Productions and based on Esther Forbes's novel of the same name.\n- Johnny Tremain retells the years in Boston, Massachusetts before the outbreak of the American Revolution.\n- Walt Disney initialized Magic Kingdom, and WED Enterprises designed it.\n- Magic Kingdom's layout and attractions are based on Disneyland Park in Anaheim, California.\n- Magic Kingdom is dedicated to fairy tales and Disney characters.",
